/T (7. Late Submissions and Extenuating Circumstances  Assessmentssubmitted after the published deadlinewill bemarked as late and will receive a penalty, unless you have approved Extenuating Circumstances \(EC\).  You may submit up to seven calendar days after the deadline, but a penalty of 5% of the  total marks available will be applied to the assessment for each 24-hour period \(or part  of it\) that the work is late \(e.g., five marks deducted each day from a total of 100\).  After seven calendar days, the assessment will be recorded as a non-submission and  given a mark of zero.  For more information, you can find the latest Assessment Handbook and Extenuating  Circumstances policy via the QMUL policies page:  https://www.qmul.ac.uk/governance-and-legal-services/policy/policies-by-category/.   )
